# Removed from launchd.plist (kept in launchd-disabled.plist, restorable): ONLY jobs for hardware the Galaxy S9 does not have.
# Policy since 18 Nov 2026 (owner: "keep iOS as intact and clean as possible, we want to fix services, not remove them"): every other
# iOS 27 daemon runs. One that crashes or burns CPU gets a fix (kernel or root step) or a task, never a trim (docs/ios27/FULLROOT.md).
# Substring of the job key or Label, one per line, with the reason.
CommCenter                            # CommCenter, -noncellular, MobileHelper, RootHelper: Apple's baseband stack (the S9's Shannon modem is driven by tools/ios27/modem)
fairplayd                             # fairplayd.H2 and fairplaydeviceidentityd: FairPlay keys live in Apple's Secure Enclave (no SEP)
security.cryptexd                     # personalised cryptexes need the SEP/AP ticket chain (no SEP, no img4 personalisation)
com.apple.securityresearchdeviceinit  # Security Research Device fusing: Apple SoC fuses only
com.apple.aned                        # Apple Neural Engine host (no ANE); CoreML falls back to CPU/GPU without it
com.apple.nearbyd                     # Ultra Wideband (no U1/UWB chip): SIGSEGV loop without it
com.apple.appledepthd                 # TrueDepth/LiDAR depth camera (none on the S9); on demand only
com.apple.watchdogd                   # Apple's AppleARMWatchDogTimer (the S9's watchdog is the kernel's own)
com.apple.wifip2pd                    # AWDL (Apple Wireless Direct Link): the S9's Broadcom firmware has no AWDL; exit loop every 10 s
com.apple.replicatord                 # companion replication over AWDL/Apple peer links (needs AWDL above)
bluetoothd                            # NOT hardware-less: Apple's bluetoothd is replaced by the hakios-inject one (92-audio-bt puts it back)
